---
import NoteFigure from './NoteFigure.astro';
const gradientCurve = Array.from({ length: 61 }, (_, i) => {
  const norm = i / 30;
  return `${i === 0 ? 'M' : 'L'} ${50 + norm * 110} ${230 - (norm - 1) ** 2 * 120}`;
}).join(' ');
---

<NoteFigure
  label="Constraint sketch"
  title="Control the critic through inputs or through weights"
  caption="Left: the WGAN-GP penalty divided by λ, as a function of a sampled input-gradient norm. It favors norm 1 and also penalizes smaller norms. Right: a unit circle mapped by W = diag(3, 1.5), then by W / 3. Spectral normalization sets the largest directional stretch to 1 for this exact linear map; a full neural network needs its other layers and operators checked too."
>
  <div class="lipschitz-panels">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 320 340" role="img" aria-labelledby="wgan-gp-title wgan-gp-desc">
      <title id="wgan-gp-title">Gradient penalty targets a norm of one at sampled inputs</title>
      <desc id="wgan-gp-desc">The normalized penalty is a parabola in the gradient norm, minimized at norm one. Both norms below and above one incur a positive penalty. This regularizer is evaluated at sampled interpolated inputs.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="wgan-gp-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="arrow-head" />
        </marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="160" y="22" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">Gradient penalty</text>
      <text x="160" y="45" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Sample interpolated inputs x̂</text>
      <path d="M 50 86 V 230 H 282" class="axis" />
      <text x="50" y="80" class="muted">penalty / λ</text>
      <text x="36" y="114" text-anchor="end" class="muted">1</text>
      <text x="36" y="234" text-anchor="end" class="muted">0</text>
      <path d={gradientCurve} class="curve" />
      {[0, 1, 2].map((tick) => (
        <g>
          <path d={`M ${50 + tick * 110} 230 v 5`} class="axis" />
          <text x={50 + tick * 110} y="255" text-anchor="middle">{tick}</text>
        </g>
      ))}
      <circle cx="160" cy="230" r="4" class="point" />
      <text x="160" y="279" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">input-gradient norm ‖∇f(x̂)‖₂</text>
      <path d="M 178 163 C 167 176, 163 198, 162 219" class="annotation" marker-end="url(#wgan-gp-arrow)" />
      <text x="185" y="156" class="accent">target: 1</text>
      <text x="160" y="310" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Penalty: (norm − 1)²</text>
      <text x="160" y="333" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">A soft constraint at sampled points</text>
    </svg>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 320 340" role="img" aria-labelledby="wgan-sn-title wgan-sn-desc">
      <title id="wgan-sn-title">Spectral normalization controls the maximum linear stretch</title>
      <desc id="wgan-sn-desc">A unit circle is mapped to an ellipse with major radius three and minor radius one point five by the diagonal matrix W. After division by its largest singular value three, the ellipse has major radius one and minor radius one half, fitting within the unit circle.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="wgan-sn-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="arrow-head" />
        </marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="160" y="22" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">Spectral normalization</text>
      <text x="160" y="45" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Rescale a weight matrix</text>
      <path d="M 45 158 H 275 M 160 95 V 220" class="axis" />
      <circle cx="160" cy="158" r="35" class="unit-circle" />
      <ellipse cx="160" cy="158" rx="105" ry="52.5" class="unnormalized" />
      <ellipse cx="160" cy="158" rx="35" ry="17.5" class="normalized" />
      <path d="M 164 158 H 262" class="annotation" marker-end="url(#wgan-sn-arrow)" />
      <text x="232" y="180" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">stretch 3</text>
      <path d="M 84 86 L 93 115" class="annotation" marker-end="url(#wgan-sn-arrow)" />
      <text x="80" y="80" text-anchor="middle">W = diag(3, 1.5)</text>
      <path d="M 112 247 C 128 223, 142 191, 156 177" class="annotation" marker-end="url(#wgan-sn-arrow)" />
      <text x="112" y="269" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">W / 3</text>
      <path d="M 251 247 C 237 224, 211 195, 186 183" class="guide" />
      <text x="251" y="269" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">unit circle</text>
      <text x="160" y="310" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Maximum stretch after rescaling: 1</text>
      <text x="160" y="333" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">A layerwise operator argument</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
</NoteFigure>

<style>
  .lipschitz-panels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 360px; height: auto; margin-inline: auto; }
  text { fill: var(--ink); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 14px; }
  .panel-title { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; }
  .muted { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .accent { fill: var(--accent); }
  .axis { fill: none; stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1; }
  .annotation, .arrow-head { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .guide { fill: none; stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1; }
  .curve { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 2; }
  .point { fill: var(--accent); }
  .unit-circle { fill: none; stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 3 3; }
  .unnormalized { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.6; }
  .normalized { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.6; }
  @container (max-width: 580px) { .lipschitz-panels { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; } }
</style>
